meaning like religion or other things, but they wouldn't be happy. So you can't have meaning without being happy. And presumably it's the opposite also true. So I'm writing a book on the decline of religion where I'm exploring the idea of affluenza. So affluenza is this interesting phenomenon of wealthy societies that are not religious, but also there is this feeling of sense of loss of meaning. But these are also the same societies that are also quite happy. So they score high on happiness levels, but they score low on meaning levels.

